{# The footer — ONE for every email (operator 2026-10-05: "all of them have the same header and
   footer styling; it's really just the content in between that changes"). Each template sets
   `footer_reason` — why this person got this email — and includes this.

   Unsubscribe + Manage notifications appear only when the envelope HAS an unsubscribe link: the
   sign-in email is transactional (no consent to withdraw) and the renderer gives it an empty one.
   Footer links are muted, not amber — they are actions, but deliberately quiet ones. #}
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="border-top:1px solid #1e2739;margin-top:8px;">
  <tr><td style="padding-top:20px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#6b7488;">
    {% if footer_reason is defined and footer_reason %}
    <p style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#6b7488;">{{ footer_reason }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if unsubscribe_url %}
    <p style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#6b7488;"><a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:#acb2c2;text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a> · one click, no sign-in needed · <a href="{{ app_origin }}/profile?tab=account" style="color:#acb2c2;text-decoration:underline;">Manage notifications</a></p>
    {% endif %}
    <p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-family:ui-monospace,'SF Mono',Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7488;">Close Listening · Listen. Understand. Remember.</p>
  </td></tr>
</table>
